n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t<div class=\"wds-tab__content wds-is-current\">\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"Island\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Finlay Island</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"Shop\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Shop</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">The Oak Depot</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"Price\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Price</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">$2,525</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"Function\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Function</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">The only way to play the Vinyls</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\n\t\t\t<div class=\"wds-tab__content\">\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"Version Added\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Version Added</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">?</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Date Added</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">?</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\n\t</section>\n\n\n\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span></h2>\n<p>The <strong class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Blue Vinyl Player</strong>  is the only way to play the Vinyls in the game.  You put a Vinyl in there and it will play the music around your entire property! but then you leave your property the sound stops playing. If you reset the area it plays at, you gotta put it where you want it to play music or around your entire base again.\n</p><p>As of 10-3-2024 there are 19 vinyls available to be purchase and used on the Vinyl Player, with 3 limited discs available through trading or the Halloween event.\n</p><p>The player can also be interacted with via the <a href=\"/wiki/Interactor\" title=\"Interactor\">Interactor</a>. A value of 0 will stop the song, a value of 5 will start playing the song, and any other value will eject the vinyl. There is an option ''Define Region''. that is the region the music plays at. if you remove that region, the music wont play where you removed it. this way, you can make different vrevs in your base have different music.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260903125032\nCache expiry: 2592000\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.080 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 65/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 55/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 1/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 45/5000000 bytes\nLua time usage: 0.005/7.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 1019459/104857600 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   74.673      1 Template:Objects\n100.00%   74.673      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key 1.43.9_prod_oaklands:pcache:idhash:963-0!sseVary=RegularPage!FandomDesktop!LegacyGalleries and timestamp 20260903125032 and revision id 21452. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>","categories":["Structures"],"links":[{"title":"Interactor","exists":true}],"images":["Unboxed_Vinyl_Player.png","Blue_Vinyl_Player.png"]}
